                <head>196. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On March 3, Loftus Becker sent to Acting Secretary Herter a memorandum entitled
                    “Questions Relating to Berlin Contingency Planning,” which covered the legal
                    aspects of planning for Berlin. (Eisenhower Library, Whitman File,
                    Administration Series)</p>
            </div>
